m both normal tax and surtax. \\\"Partially\\\" tax-exempt securities are those with the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [742, 1003, 1401, 1328], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"income exempt from the normal tax except that in the case of partial tax-exempt Treasury bonds, interest derived from $5,000 of principal amount owned by any one holder is also exempt from the surtax. \\\"Taxable\\\" securities are those with the income subject to normal tax and surtax.\\n9/ Includes F. H. A. debentures; see footnote 10.\\n10/ A small indeterminate amount of these debentures is partially tax-exempt.\\n11/ Includes $70,0 million depository bonds held by commercial banks not included in the Treasury Survey.\\n12/ C. C. C. demand obligations as of the close of the previous month in the amount of $268 thousand, all held by commercial banks, are shown only in the total amount outstanding; holdings by reporting banks are not available.\\n13/ Exclude issues completely held by Farm Credit Administration agencies. The proprietary interest of the United States in these banks ended on June 26, 1947.\\n* Less than $500,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [51, 18, 83, 40], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"40\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1224, 2, 1475, 53], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [537, 82, 993, 115], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"MARKET QUOTATIONS, NOVEMBER 28, 1952\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [58, 144, 715, 442], \"page_id\": 52}], \"content\": \"Current market quotations shown here are over-the-counter closing quotations in the New York market for the last trading day of the month, as reported to the Treasury by the Federal Reserve Bank 