 fifteen or more years to maturity or first call. 2/ Average revised beginning April 1, 1947. Old average for April 1947 was 2.47%. 3/ As of December 21, 1949, the Consolidated Gas Electric Light and Power Company of Baltimore 2-3/4% of 1961 were dropped from the average, having been called. 4/ As of October 20, 1950, the Standard Oil Company of California 2-3/4% of 1965-66 were dropped from the average, having been called. 5/ The long-term taxable Treasury bond average was revised beginning April 1, 1952 (see \\\"Note\\\"). The old average for April 1952 was 2.62 percent. 6/ Market closed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [59, 329, 107, 1678], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"AVERAGE YIELDS OF LONG-TERM TREASURY AND CORPORATE BONDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [102, 880, 143, 1120], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Monthly Series\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [5, 24, 176, 68], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"January 1955\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1365, 31, 1411, 68], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"45\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 99, 945, 128], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"YIELDS OF TREASURY AND CORPORATE BONDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [158, 172, 1301, 1841], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1327, 1385, 1348, 1830], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Office of the Secretary of the Treasury, Office of the Technical Staff\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1315, 823, 1328, 1224], \"page_id\": 57}], \"content\": \"Page 1 of 2\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"t