nt\": \"JUN 23 1972\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [968, 1414, 1365, 1461], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"TREASURY DEPARTMENT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [141, 1614, 1305, 1687], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"UNITED STATES TREASURY DEPARTMENT\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 1687, 1310, 1733], \"page_id\": 7}], \"content\": \"OFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [17, 26, 198, 53], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"January 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [533, 200, 907, 233], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Table of Contents\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1128, 314, 1196, 347], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Page\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [237, 360, 1207, 1500], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Treasury financing operations</td><td>A-1</td></tr><tr><td>Summary of Federal fiscal operations</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Budget receipts and expenditures</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Trust account and other transactions</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury cash income and outgo</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Debt outstanding and general fund</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Statutory debt limitation</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>Debt operations</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>United States savings bonds</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury savings notes</td><td>23</td></tr><tr><td>Ownership of Federal securities</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>Treasury survey of ownership of Federal securities</td><td>26</td></tr><tr><td>Market quotations on Treasury securities</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>Average yields of long-term bonds</td><td>33</td></tr><tr><td>Internal revenue collections</td><td>35</td></tr><tr><td>Monetary statistics</td><td>39</td></tr><tr><td>Capital movements</td><td>43</td></tr><tr><td>Corporations and certain other business-type activities -- balance sheets (inlcuing loans by type)</td><td>56</td></tr><tr><td>Cumulative table of contents</td><td>73</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [239, 1544, 1101, 1634], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Note: Where calculations have been made from un-rounded figures, the details may not check to the totals shown.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [55, 20, 234, 53], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"January 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1422, 20, 1456, 37], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"A-1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [545, 176, 976, 204], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Treasury Financing Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [120, 314, 483, 338], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Maturing F and G Savings Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [121, 345, 714, 551], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"On December 11, 1953, the Treasury invited holders of those Series F and G savings bonds which begin to mature in January 1954 to exchange them at maturity for other series of savings bonds. The statement added that at this time the Treasury was not offering to holders of these maturing bonds any Treasury issue other than savings bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [121, 589, 716, 973], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"It was pointed out that individual owners of the maturing Series F and G bonds may make reinvestment in Series E and H bonds up to the $20,000 annual limits on each of these series. Not only individuals, but any other holders of these maturing bonds may reinvest in Series J and K bonds, which have a combined annual limitation of $200,000 issue price. These transactions will be handled at Federal Reserve Banks and branches and at the Office of the Treasurer of the United States in Washington. Holders of the maturing bonds may submit them, for either exchange or cash payment, direct or through their banks after having the request for payment\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [125, 1015, 711, 1074], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Note: Details of Treasury market financing operations are shown elsewhere in this issue of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\", in the tables on \\\"Offerings\\\" and \\\"Dis-\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [827, 314, 1415, 365], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"certified, which can be done at any bank or post office.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 406, 1415, 637], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"In the case of Series G bonds, the final interest due on the maturity date will be paid with the principal. No interest will accrue on bonds of either Series F or G after maturity. In order to avoid loss of interest on their investment, holders should submit the bonds from twenty to thirty days in advance of their maturity dates, whether for cash redemption or for new bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [835, 679, 1194, 701], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Treasury 91-Day Bills Refunded\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [835, 707, 1417, 936], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Maturities of 91-day Treasury bills totaled $7.5 billion in December. They were refunded in full by weekly offerings in amounts equivalent to the $1.5 billion maturing. The average rates of discount on the new offerings were 1.589 percent for December 3; 1.603 percent for December 10; 1.682 percent for December 17; 1.704 percent for December 24; and 1.574 percent for December 31.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 1015, 1418, 1072], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"position\\\", respectively, of marketable issues of bonds, notes, and certificates of indebtedness, and in the table \\\"Offerings of Treasury Bills\\\".\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [32, 22, 223, 59], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"January 1954\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1408, 29, 1453, 64], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [502, 90, 968, 125], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"SUMMARY OF FEDERAL FISCAL OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [616, 141, 855, 180], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [27, 174, 1443, 1619], \"page_id\": 13}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Budget receipts and expenditures</th><th>Net of trust account and other transactions 2/ 3/</th><th>Clearing account 4/</th><th>Net increase in public debt, or decrease (-)</th><th>Net increase in general fund balance, or decrease (-)</th><th>General fund balance</th><th colspan=\\\"4\\\">Levels, and of period</th></tr><tr><th></th><th>Net receipts 1/</th><th>Expenditures 2/</th><th>Surplus, or deficit (-) 2/</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th>Public debt</th><th>Guaranteed securities</th><th>Total Federal securities</th><th>Subject to limitation 5/</th></tr><tr><td>Fiscal years:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td